<title>USA: USDA July 11 world grain highlights.</title>
<headline>USDA July 11 world grain highlights.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>World grain production will total 1,864.38 million tonnes in 1997/98, up from 1,855.05 million tonnes estimated last month, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday.</p>
<p>World output would include 586.83 million tonnes of wheat, 898.17 million of coarse (feed) grains and 379.38 million of rice. Oilseeds were pegged at 275.26 million tonnes.  </p>
<p>In its first estimate of the 1997/98 soybean crop in Brazil and Argentina, USDA projected Brazil's harvest at 28.00 million tonnes and Argentina at 13.90 million.</p>
<p>Soybean exports in 1997/98 from Brazil and Argentina were estimated at 7.00 million tonnes and 1.50 million, respectively.</p>
<p>USDA forecast Brazil 1997/98 soybean imports at 2.25 million tonnes, up sharply from 800,000 tonnes in 1996/97.</p>
<p>Brazil's 1996/97 soybean crop was estimated at 26.50 million tonnes and exports were put at 7.85 million tonnes.  </p>
<p>China's imports during 1997/98 were estimated at 1.55 million tonnes of soyoil, 3.00 million of soymeal, 2.25 million of soybeans and 3.50 million of wheat. In the same period, it was forecast to export 2.00 million tonnes of corn.</p>
<p>The EU wheat crop this year was forecast at 98.55 million tonnes, up from 97.85 million estimated last month.</p>
<p>EU wheat exports in 1997/98 were forecast for 30.73 million tonnes. Exports from other major world competitors were estimated at 18.50 million for Canada and 13.50 million for Australia.  </p>
